1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Listen to a talk in an economics class.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:07,203
Professor: Behavioral economics is a field that combines insights from psychology

3
00:00:07,203 --> 00:00:11,230
and economics to understand how people make economic decisions.

4
00:00:11,230 --> 00:00:16,101
Unlike traditional economics, which assumes that individuals act rationally,

5
00:00:16,101 --> 00:00:24,220
behavioral economics recognizes that people often behave irrationally due to cognitive biases and emotional factors.

6
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:28,745
One key concept in behavioral economics is the idea of heuristics,

7
00:00:28,745 --> 00:00:33,270
which are mental shortcuts that people use to make decisions quickly.

8
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:36,280
While heuristics can be helpful

9
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:39,240
they can also lead to systematic errors in judgment.

10
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:46,861
For example, the availability heuristic causes people to overestimate the likelihood of events that are widely reported,

11
00:00:46,861 --> 00:00:52,240
such as plane crashes, while underestimating more common risks like car accidents.

12
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:54,902
Another important concept is loss aversion,

13
00:00:54,902 --> 00:01:02,000
which suggests that people experience the pain of loss more intensely than the pleasure of gain.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,258
This can lead to risk-averse behavior,

15
00:01:04,258 --> 00:01:09,150
where individuals are more likely to avoid losses than to pursue equivalent gains.

16
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:13,561
For instance, investors might hold onto losing stocks for too long,

17
00:01:13,561 --> 00:01:17,170
hoping they will rebound, rather than cutting their losses.

18
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:25,060
Understanding these and other behavioral biases can help policymakers design better economic policies and interventions.

19
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:27,103
Next, we will examine how nudges,

20
00:01:27,103 --> 00:01:30,040
or subtle changes in the way choices are presented

21
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,210
can help people reach better decisions.
